<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>The Church from her dear Master</l><l>Received the gift divine,</l><l>And still that light she lifteth</l><l>O’er all the earth to shine:</l><l>It is the golden treasure</l><l>Where gems of truth are stored;</l><l>It is the heaven-drawn picture</l><l>Of Christ, the living Word.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>It floateth like a banner</l><l>Before God’s host unfurled;</l><l>It shineth like a beacon</l><l>Above the darkling world;</l><l>It is the chart and compass</l><l>That, o’er life’s surging sea,</l><l>’Mid mists and rocks and quicksands</l><l>Still guide, O Christ, to Thee.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>O make Thy Church, dear Savior,</l><l>A lampstand of pure gold,</l><l>To bear before the nations</l><l>Thy light, that all behold;</l><l>O teach Thy wandering pilgrims</l><l>By this their path to trace,</l><l>Till, clouds and darkness ended,</l><l>They see Thee face to ace.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
